#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0155 expect=violation domain=APZZ
#expectViolationCount 1
#note "DOMAIN is 4 characters and begins with `AP`, so the first disjunct is false and the whole rule turns on the codelist lookup: `suffix(\"APZZ\", 2)` = `ZZ`, which is NOT a published SDTM domain abbreviation, so the second disjunct fires. This is the scenario that proves the `codelist_terms` membership test is live rather than vacuous — flip `ZZ` to any term in the list below and it must go green. ⚠⚠ The `#library codelist-terms DOMAIN` line MUST carry real 2-letter SDTM SUBMISSION VALUES (`AE`, `CM`, `VS`, `LB`), never NCI C-codes: with C-codes in that list every conformant AP-- dataset would fire and this scenario would pass for the wrong reason. The CDISC-CG0001 / CORE-000929 fixtures are the pattern to FOLLOW, not to avoid: they were re-authored in ca63ebf5 and now split the three channels properly — submission values on `#library codelist-terms`, NCI C-codes on `#library codelist-term-ccodes`, the codelist's own ccode / preferred term on `#library codelist-meta`. Copy that shape if this fixture ever needs C-codes. ⚠ The rule's operation declares `returntype=\"value\"` and coreJ HONOURS the parameter (ca63ebf5), so `codelist_terms` yields term submission values here by contract rather than by accident — which is why the list below must be submission values. See plans/PLAN-codelist-terms-returntype.md."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-3
#library codelist-terms DOMAIN AE CM VS LB
dataset APZZ label="Associated Persons Unknown Parent"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col APID    type=Char label="Associated Persons Identifier"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | APZZ | AP-701-1015
